   226	## Act 3: depth, and changing your mind
   227	
   228	### Ask what a scientist asks
   229	
   230	A reviewer reading a physics or algorithms paper asks specific questions.
   231	What is the equation, and in which regime? What are the boundary
   232	conditions? What is the complexity, under which assumptions? GND answers
   233	each one from a reviewed passage, or says **unknown** when the paper does
   234	not support an answer.
   235	
   236	| Paper | Question | Answer |
   237	|---|---|---|
   238	| Shallow-water dam break | equation and regime | supported |
   239	| | boundary treatment | supported |
   240	| | discretization | supported |
   241	| | measured conservation residual | **unknown**: the run reports none |
   242	| Alanine dipeptide, OPES-eABF | system and force field | supported |
   243	| | sampling objective | supported |
   244	| | numerical approximation | supported |
   245	| | does it hold in another solvent? | **unknown**: the run is in vacuum |
   246	| Randomized SVD | operator and objective | supported |
   247	| | algorithm components | supported |
   248	| | complexity with its assumptions | supported: O(mn log(k)) flops, dense input |
   249	| | run time on an H100 | **unknown**: no benchmark reported |
   250	
   251	"Unknown" is an answer. It says the question was asked and the paper
   252	does not answer it. That is different from a question nobody asked.
   253	
   254	Numbers stay exact, too. One source gives the same time step as
   255	`2 fs`, `0.002 ps` and `0.000002 ns`, and also mentions `2 eV` and
   256	`0.0001 ps`. GND records the step as exactly `0.002 ps`, ties it to the
   257	second line, proves the value, and replays the proof.
   258	
   259	### Read again, and find more each time
   260	
   261	One quick read of a paper misses things. The method details sit in the
   262	methods section, and a limitation sits in a closing sentence. So the agent
   263	reads in passes. Each pass goes after the questions that are still open,
   264	and GND checks each pass before its facts are kept.
   265	
   266	The example is a molecular simulation study with seven questions: the
   267	system, the method, any stated denial, an alternative integrator, a method
   268	in the annex, an equation, and an older form of the method question.
   269	
   270	**You ask**
   271	
   272	```text
   273	Read the alanine study with /gnd:gnd-extract in passes. Start with a broad
   274	read of each source's opening. Then go back only to the sections that can
   275	answer the questions still open, and stop when every required question has
   276	an answer or a reason it has none.
   277	```
   278	
   279	**What each pass added**
   280	
   281	| Pass | Sections read | What the agent returned | Facts kept so far |
   282	|---|---|---|---|
   283	| 1. Broad | study opening, annex opening, a withheld table | 1 answer, 1 empty, 1 refusal | **2**: the subject's label and the system, *alanine dipeptide in vacuum* |
   284	| 2. Targeted | study methods, study limits | 2 answers | **4**: adds *Langevin integration at 300 K with 2 fs steps* and *no barostat* |
   285	| 3. Review | none | proposes a new vocabulary term, *method family* | 4, and the study opening goes back on the list to re-read under the new term |
   286	
   287	The targeted pass found two more facts and answered two more questions.
   288	It read 234 bytes in all, so the run reports its yield as 2 new facts per
   289	234 bytes read. The agent was called 3 times in the broad pass and 2 times
   290	in the targeted pass. A refused or empty answer is recorded as refused or
   291	empty, and never as "nothing there".
   292	
   293	A candidate can also be stopped before it is kept. A separate report gave the same molecule
   294	two different labels. GND's verify and check steps both rejected that
   295	candidate, so it never joined the kept facts.
   296	
   297	**Know what was not read.** When the run stops, each question has exactly
   298	one disposition:
   299	
   300	| Question | Section | Read? | Disposition |
   301	|---|---|---|---|
   302	| system | study opening | yes | supported |
   303	| method | study methods | yes | supported |
   304	| denial | study limits | yes | **explicitly denied** |
   305	| alternative | study methods | yes | **read, not found** |
   306	| annex method | annex methods | no | **unavailable** |
   307	| equation | control equation | no | **not applicable** |
   308	
   309	"Read, not found", "unavailable" and "denied" no longer look alike.
   310	"Read, not found" is only allowed when the reading is good enough to
   311	trust. Scored against an independent answer, the extraction found 2 of 2
   312	facts, so the
   313	absence of an alternative integrator counts, scoped to the methods
   314	section. At 1 of 2, the same absence would be reported as unavailable.
   315	
   316	Every pass is saved with its inputs, so the whole run replays later
   317	without calling the reading agent again.
