    30	## The scoring rule
    31	
    32	This section is the rule's one home.
    33	
    34	- A produced row is **found** when one gold fact of the same document has
    35	  the same fact type and the same role values, and the section the row was
    36	  read from is one of the sections that gold fact is anchored in. Values
    37	  are compared after Unicode NFC, case folding and collapsing whitespace,
    38	  and nothing else: a spelling the gold does not use is not found.
    39	- A row is **wrong predicate** when a gold fact anchored in that section
    40	  has the same values under another fact type.
    41	- Each gold fact is found at most once. Every produced row counts in
    42	  precision, including rows outside every gold fact's sections.
    43	- **Precision** per pass is found rows over produced rows. **Recall after a
    44	  pass** is the gold facts found so far over all gold facts.
    45	
    46	The grain is the section: a produced fact has no span of its own, only its
    47	section's. Scores taken at a finer grain, a quote's span, are not directly
    48	comparable.
