     1	# Literature regression corpus
     2	
     3	A small public corpus for measuring how well a literature pipeline reads
     4	scientific papers. A staged assurance report scores a run of that pipeline
     5	against an answer key, and keeps each stage's denominator separate. It is the
     6	public reconstruction of the known-error set in issue 193, part 1. Larger
     7	sets stay with whoever owns them, and can be scored with the same report.
     8	
     9	The documents are **synthetic paraphrases** of public works, written for
    10	regression testing. Each names its work's public identifier, and each
    11	identifier was checked against its public record on 2026-11-15. No document
    12	is the text of its work.
    13	
    14	This directory is the entry point, and it holds no labels. The answers are in
    15	[`answers/`](answers/), kept apart so the corpus can be handed to a reader
    16	without them.
    17	
    18	## What is here
    19	
    20	| Path | What it is |
    21	|---|---|
    22	| `model.orm.yaml` | The flat corpus model. A method is identified by the name a document uses, as in the host graph the issue reports |
    23	| `corpus/corpus.json` | The corpus manifest (`literature-corpus/1`): documents, their digests and splits, and every passage |
    24	| `corpus/documents/*.md` | One document per work: a title line, an identifier line, then one passage per line |
    25	| `corpus/artifacts/` | `gnd extract` output for the model, which `gnd fidelity` needs |
    26	| `runs/reference/` | The faithful reference run (`literature-run/1`). It must score exit 0 |
    27	| `expected/` | The approved expected outcome of each scored case (`literature-assurance-expectation/1`) |
    28	| `answers/` | The answer key, gold populations and renderer manifests. Not for blind readers |
    29	
    30	Every generated file is rebuilt, byte for byte, by
    31	`tools/build_literature_example.py` in the source repository.
